#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Generate the comparison from retained measurements; never invent missing scores."""
import html
import json
from pathlib import Path

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
OUT=ROOT/'docs/performance/five-models'
summary=json.loads((OUT/'summary.json').read_text())
names={'phonon':'Phonon 31M · q8 CPU','sopro':'Sopro v2 Turbo · int8 CPU','qwen3':'Qwen3 Ryan · 4-bit MLX','cosyvoice3':'CosyVoice3 · 4-bit MLX port','voxcpm2':'VoxCPM2 · 4-bit MLX'}
lines=['# Five local TTS configurations','', 'Measured 2026-10-30 on Apple M4, 16 GB, macOS 27.2. **All 50 recordings completed, contained finite audible PCM, had no clipped samples, and scored zero word errors in the local Whisper small.en screen on one shared 24-word passage.** This is not a listening study or a broad pronunciation test. No model is adopted as a quality winner.','', 'Five interleaved rounds, one fresh process per model per round; each process performs a first inference and a warm inference. The table summarizes the five warm inferences. Startup means the first materialized PCM chunk, excluding physical playback. No claim of M1/macOS 14 certification.','', '| Configuration | First PCM, median [range] | Full synthesis, median | RTF | Peak process RSS | MLX peak allocation |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for m in summary['models']:
 a=m['warm_first_chunk_ms'];g=m['warm_generation_ms'];s=lambda x:f'{x/1000:.3f} s' if x>=1000 else f'{x:.1f} ms'
 lines.append(f"| {names[m['model']]} | {s(a['median'])} [{s(a['min'])}–{s(a['max'])}] | {s(g['median'])} | {m['warm_rtf']['median']:.3f} | {m['peak_rss_bytes']/1e6:.0f} MB | {m['mlx_peak_bytes']/1e6:.0f} MB |")
lines += ['', 'RTF = generation seconds / audio seconds; below 1 means faster than playback. RSS and MLX allocation overlap; **do not add them**. MLX allocation is included because process RSS alone understates the larger pipelines. Load time includes Python imports, materialized model parameters, and preparation of the reference when applicable. New process is not an uncached disk or full application cold-start measurement.','', '## What the measurements support','', '- Phonon is a compact, fast candidate in this configuration. Its prebuilt runtime targets macOS 15+, so the app’s macOS 14 baseline still requires a source-built runtime and validation.', '- Sopro streams promptly but its assets, ready memory, and peak memory exceed the original mandatory-model resource limits. Its CPU int8 configuration has not been compared against a tuned MPS configuration.', '- Qwen CustomVoice streams in 0.5-second output chunks. The first inference is slower than warm generation; load and first inference are retained separately. The selected checkpoint offers preset Ryan plus instructions; it is not the Base cloning or VoiceDesign checkpoint.', '- CosyVoice and VoxCPM2 returned only one PCM chunk for this input in the tested adapters. Their startup includes the whole utterance generation. Do not transfer advertised streaming latency from another runtime to these results.', '- VoxCPM2 retains a 62.9-second warm-start outlier. No slow trial was discarded. The current test does not establish its cause or a stable tail-latency guarantee.', '- All larger candidates remain optional experimental local profiles. The original native default remains available; initial required downloads and release budgets have not been redefined.', '', '## Native integration','', 'All five profiles passed one production Reader → PCM conversion → real CPAL callback → stop smoke test. These smoke tests include concurrent development/profiling activity and are **behavior verification, not comparative performance results**. See `app-voice-9.jsonl` through `app-voice-13.jsonl`. Their RSS values cover the Rust host, not the model subprocess.', '', 'The bridge keeps selected text and audio in memory, disables Hub/transformer networking during inference, suppresses backend text logs, and validates registered asset/script hashes before loading. One model is loaded at a time. Esc/replace cancels the active run; if inference must be aborted, the subprocess is terminated and the selected model reloads in the background. This recovery can make the next reading cold. Only Phonon and Sopro currently meet the original component startup target in every measured warm trial; the user has allowed higher startup latency for quality candidates. No acoustic or M1 performance certification is implied.', '', 'Native playback converts all profiles to 24 kHz and uses pinned Apache-2.0 Sonic for pitch-preserving 0.75×–2× tempo. Model component timings above exclude the IPC/tempo/EQ/UI pipeline. Capability filters describe documented checkpoint capabilities; emotion/design/dialogue authoring controls are not exposed by these reading profiles.', '', '## Reproduce locally','', '```sh', 'uv venv --python 3.12 .cache/advanced-tts-env', 'uv pip sync --python .cache/advanced-tts-env/bin/python docs/performance/five-models/requirements-main.txt', 'uv venv --python 3.12 .cache/cosyvoice-tts-env', 'uv pip sync --python .cache/cosyvoice-tts-env/bin/python docs/performance/five-models/requirements-cosyvoice.txt', 'python3 scripts/prepare_advanced_tts.py', '# Clone the Cosy port at the exact commit recorded in five-model-runtime-notes.md.', '# Restore the synthetic reference.wav matching reference.json and its retained SHA-256.', 'python3 scripts/register_advanced_tts.py', 'python3 scripts/benchmark_advanced_tts.py', '.cache/voice-eval-env/bin/python scripts/check_advanced_tts_audio.py', 'python3 scripts/report_advanced_tts.py', '```', '', 'The registration is local development configuration (`~/Library/Application Support/InfoTransfer/experimental-runtimes.json`). It points at these virtual environments and verified caches. The 45 MB development bundle does not include Python, heavy model weights, or the reference voice. Runtimes and packaging remain release work. Do not distribute the cache as a certified release: model-conversion/auxiliary asset notices and the macOS 14 runtime build still need release review.', '', '## Evidence and sources','', '- `protocol.json`, `runs.jsonl`, `summary.json`, `asr.jsonl`, all 50 retained WAVs and backend logs. Generation and scoring consume actual PCM; WAV hashes are checked before ASR.', '- `downloads.json` pins every staged model artifact, byte count and SHA-256; the requirement freezes identify the runtime environments.', '- [Verified capability and setup notes](../../five-model-runtime-notes.md) contain primary-source links and conditional feature definitions.', '- [Qwen3](https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3-TTS), [VoxCPM2](https://github.com/OpenBMB/VoxCPM), [CosyVoice3](https://github.com/QwenAudio/CosyVoice), [Sopro](https://github.com/samuel-vitorino/sopro), [Phonon](https://github.com/gradium-ai/xn-ptts).', '- [Cosy MLX port](https://github.com/DePasqualeOrg/mlx-audio-plus/tree/4c9ec6a8489e790b5ba8964ab1f1d63150476f9f); [Sonic pinned source](https://github.com/waywardgeek/sonic/tree/b93885dcb70aae50c6f76b0fe4e0868f029a077e).', '', 'Naturalness ratings from the previous native chunk policy were invalidated instead of being attached to new audio. Audition these files directly; do not interpret one-passage zero WER as a naturalness score.']
(OUT/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
data=[dict(m,name=names[m['model']]) for m in summary['models']]
page='''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;color:var(--foreground);font-family:var(--font-sans);font-size:14px}p{margin:6px 0 12px;color:var(--muted-foreground);line-height:1.5}nav{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:12px 0}button{font:inherit;color:var(--foreground);background:var(--secondary);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:7px 12px;cursor:pointer}button[aria-pressed=true]{background:var(--primary);color:var(--primary-foreground)}svg{width:100%;height:300px;overflow:visible}text{font:12px var(--font-sans);fill:var(--muted-foreground)}.label{fill:var(--foreground);font-weight:500}.row{margin:8px 0}.note{font-size:12px}a{color:var(--primary)}@media(max-width:480px){svg{height:340px}}
</style></head><body><p>Apple M4 · 16 GB · five warm runs per configuration</p><nav aria-label="Measurement"><button aria-pressed="true" data-key="first">First audio</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-key="full">Synthesis time</button><button aria-pressed="false" data-key="rss">Peak process RSS</button></nav><svg role="img" aria-label="Measured local TTS pipeline performance"></svg><p id="caption"></p><p class="note">50 recordings · no clipping · zero ASR word errors on one shared passage. Naturalness and M1 performance remain unverified. RSS excludes some shared GPU allocation.</p><script>
const data=DATA;const svg=document.querySelector('svg');const ns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';function node(type,attrs,text){let n=document.createElementNS(ns,type);Object.entries(attrs).forEach(([k,v])=>n.setAttribute(k,v));if(text)n.textContent=text;svg.append(n);return n}function draw(key){svg.innerHTML='';svg.setAttribute('viewBox','0 0 700 300');let left=230,right=670;let max=key==='rss'?3000:100000;let x=v=>left+(right-left)*(key==='rss'?v/max:Math.log10(Math.max(1,v))/5);let ticks=key==='rss'?[0,1000,2000,3000]:[1,10,100,1000,10000,100000];ticks.forEach(v=>{node('line',{x1:x(v),x2:x(v),y1:12,y2:252,stroke:'var(--border)'});node('text',{x:x(v),y:275,'text-anchor':'middle'},key==='rss'?v+' MB':v<1000?v+' ms':v/1000+' s')});data.forEach((m,i)=>{let y=35+i*47;let r=key==='first'?m.warm_first_chunk_ms:key==='full'?m.warm_generation_ms:null;let mid=r?r.median:m.peak_rss_bytes/1e6;node('text',{x:0,y:y-4,class:'label'},m.name);node('text',{x:0,y:y+13},key==='rss'?mid.toFixed(0)+' MB':mid<1000?mid.toFixed(1)+' ms':(mid/1000).toFixed(2)+' s');if(r){node('line',{x1:x(r.min),x2:x(r.max),y1:y,y2:y,stroke:'var(--chart-2)','stroke-width':3});[r.min,r.max].forEach(v=>node('line',{x1:x(v),x2:x(v),y1:y-5,y2:y+5,stroke:'var(--chart-2)'}))}node('circle',{cx:x(mid),cy:y,r:6,fill:'var(--chart-1)'})});document.getElementById('caption').textContent=key==='rss'?'Maximum observed host RSS, with a linear axis. MLX allocations overlap RSS and are reported separately in the report.':'Dots show medians; whiskers show the complete range. Time axis is logarithmic. First audio is model PCM availability, excluding capture and physical playback.';document.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',b.dataset.key===key))}document.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>draw(b.dataset.key));draw('first');
</script></body></html>'''.replace('DATA',json.dumps(data))
(OUT/'comparison.html').write_text(page)
print(str(OUT/'REPORT.md'))
